  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: A trough of low pressure will move\neastward across the Pacific Northwest this afternoon and this\nevening. This will result in the surface pressure gradient\ntightening across Northern Nevada. A High Wind Warning is in\neffect for Eastern Elko County until 11 PM PDT this evening. A\nWind Advisory is in effect for the remainder of Northern Nevada\nuntil 11 PM PDT this evening. Elevated fire weather conditions are\nexpected in most of Northern and Central Nevada this afternoon and\nthis evening due to southwest to west wind gusts near 50 mph and\nminimum relative humidity values as low as 8 percent. A few strong\nto marginally severe thunderstorms are conceivable in Northeastern\nElko County, particularly from Jackpot to West Wendover, this \nafternoon into this evening.\n\nBroad cyclonic flow aloft will prevail Thursday into the upcoming\nweekend. A cold front will swing through Northern and Central\nNevada Sunday, resulting in a slight chance of precipitation. A\ncooling trend is expected Thursday through Sunday. By Sunday\nafternoon, high temperatures will be twelve to fourteen degrees\nbelow normal for this time of year. A ridge of high pressure will\nslowly build eastward across the Silver State Monday and Tuesday,\nresulting in a warming trend.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding damaging wind gusts in Eastern Elko County this \nafternoon and this evening. High forecast confidence in strong, \ngusty winds in the remainder of Northern Nevada this afternoon and\nthis evening. High forecast confidence regarding elevated fire \nweather conditions in most of Northern and Central Nevada this \nafternoon and this evening. Low forecast confidence in a few \nstrong to marginally severe thunderstorms in Northeastern Elko \nCounty this afternoon into this evening. No deviations from the\nNBM model output.",
